## Workflow

1. Ensure the node answers: `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:9200/`.
2. Search by mechanism (not just API names), e.g. sidebar tree DnD, bookmark folders, toolbar shell tabs, GPUI overlays.
3. Prefer:

```bash
.xerj/search.sh "command palette overlay gpui"
# or
curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:9200/gitronimo-docs/_search' -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  --data-binary '{"size":8,"query":{"match":{"body":"sidebar drag drop folder"}},"highlight":{"fields":{"body":{}}},"_source":["title","ax_path","language"]}'
```

4. Catalog: `xerj autoindex map --url http://127.0.0.1:9200`
5. If retrieval returns nothing relevant, say so and implement normally.
6. Cite project + file (`ax_path`) in the commit message when you drew on a peer; state adapted vs approach-only.
7. Strongest trigger to retrieve: the same error has already been looped twice.

## Re-index (after large source changes)

Index roots separately — do **not** autoindex the monorepo root (`target/` is still walked despite ignore files on this xerj build).

```bash
URL=http://127.0.0.1:9200
P=gitronimo
B=/Users/mpak/www/rust/gitronimo/.xerj
xerj autoindex apps --url "$URL" --prefix "$P" --state-dir "$B/ai-apps" --no-semantic --no-graph
xerj autoindex crates --url "$URL" --prefix "$P" --state-dir "$B/ai-crates" --no-semantic --no-graph
xerj autoindex docs --url "$URL" --prefix "$P" --state-dir "$B/ai-docs" --no-semantic --no-graph
xerj autoindex /Users/mpak/www/rust/xerj-refs/rgitui --url "$URL" --prefix "$P" --state-dir "$B/ai-rgitui" --no-semantic --no-graph
xerj autoindex /Users/mpak/www/rust/xerj-refs/GitComet --url "$URL" --prefix "$P" --state-dir "$B/ai-GitComet" --no-semantic --no-graph
xerj autoindex /Users/mpak/www/rust/xerj-refs/gitui --url "$URL" --prefix "$P" --state-dir "$B/ai-gitui" --no-semantic --no-graph
```
